0..79 Comment "// A record type\'s faces: each a set of the record\'s labels, named in a `where`"
80..158 Comment "// block after the type. A static bracket after the type fixes some fields, by"
159..179 Comment "// label or by face."
180..182 Comment "//"
183..259 Comment "// A record type\'s labels are its boundary. A face over them names a part of"
260..339 Comment "// the record, so a later form restricts a value to that part. The patched type"
340..416 Comment "// is the record of the fields the bracket leaves free. A name at it reads a"
417..463 Comment "// fixed field as the value the bracket fixes."
464..466 Comment "//"
467..544 Comment "// The block names each face as a theory\'s `face` member does. The block ends"
545..624 Comment "// the type member at its `}`, as a `data` block ends its declaration. A record"
625..693 Comment "// type with no block keeps its labels as its boundary all the same."
694..762 Comment "// `Config[.port = 443, .tls = true]` fixes two fields by label, and"
763..839 Comment "// `Config[secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}]` fixes the face `secure`."
840..871 Comment "// `|->` spells `↦` in ASCII."
872..874 Comment "//"
875..953 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
954..1031 Comment "//   face named twice, and a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks,"
1032..1044 Comment "//   refused"
1045..1124 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1125..1135 Comment "//   faces"
1136..1214 Comment "// - owes: #5536 — a configuration coerced to a patched type, and an element"
1215..1271 Comment "//   of a patched type coerced back to the configuration"
1272..1352 Comment "// - owes: #5106 — two faces fixed at once, whose values agree where the faces"
1353..1362 Comment "//   meet"
